# Serge agent secrets — sourced by the `serge` launcher and exported into the
# agent process. Keep this file chmod 600. Do NOT commit it anywhere.
#
# ---- Web search backend -----------------------------------------------------
# Serge routes through an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, which has no native
# web_search. Set ONE search-backend key below so the WebSearch tool works.
#
# Tavily (recommended): sign up at https://app.tavily.com → copy the key.
# Free tier ~1,000 searches/month. Key looks like  tvly-xxxxxxxx
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# Optional: pin the backend so failures are loud/obvious instead of silently
# falling through to (blocked) DuckDuckGo. Leave unset to use auto mode, which
# tries Tavily first once the key above is set.
# WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER=tavily

# ---- Other backends (alternatives — only need one) --------------------------
# BRAVE_API_KEY=
# EXA_API_KEY=
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=
# JINA_API_KEY=

# ---- Hive model selection & budget (USER-SET — Serge must not self-edit; see memory) --
# Coder = DeepSeek V4 PRO (local-coder, launcher DEFAULT_MODEL); reviewer = GLM-5.2
# (qwen-coder, review-on-stop.sh's built-in default — no override needed here).
# Monthly OpenRouter budget target surfaced by /cost (cost.sh).
# Reset 65→20 on 2026-07-29 (user: "reset the cap to $20 per month"). 65 was a display-only
# "headroom" figure that DISAGREED with the thing that actually enforces: budget-watchdog.sh
# uses SERGE_MONTHLY_CAP_USD (default 20) and never lifts the monthly cap. So /cost would
# report comfortably in-budget at $50 while the watchdog had already locked the paid seats
# at $20. Display and enforcement now both say 20.
SERGE_BUDGET_USD=20
# Auto-route image/screenshot turns to the vision-capable seat (Opus / cloud-brain),
# then flip back to the coder on the next text turn (engine patch in openaiShim.ts).
# Only cloud-brain has vision; DeepSeek/GLM are text-only. Unset this to disable.
SERGE_VISION_MODEL=bedrock-brain
# Route present-day / live-result questions (scores, prices, weather, news) to the
# cloud brain — the cheap coder seats hallucinate current facts. Tight heuristic in
# openaiShim.ts (latestHumanTurnIsLiveFactQuery); flips back to the coder next turn.
# Unset to disable. Pairs with the constitution's corroborate-live-results rule.
# 2026-07-09: retargeted pro-coder → cloud-brain (user call). The 2026-06-22 move to
# pro-coder targeted DeepSeek V4 Pro; after the all-free rewire pro-coder = Gemini 3.1
# Flash-Lite — WEAKER than the Mistral workhorse, so the old target escalated DOWN.
# cloud-brain (Gemini 3.5 Flash) is the strongest free seat; its ~20 req/day free
# bucket is fine now that the shim strips <system-reminder> text before classifying
# (pre-fix, EVERY first turn would have burned this quota).
SERGE_LIVEFACT_MODEL=cloud-brain

# Extended thinking / reasoning depth (rewired 2026-07-10).
# Seats on THIS list get the native Anthropic `thinking` param from /effort
# (budgets low=1024/medium=2048/high=4096/xhigh=16384); every other seat gets
# `reasoning_effort` (xhigh clamped to high). The 2026-07-04 list
# (local-coder,pro-coder,cloud-brain,bedrock-brain) matched the old Bedrock
# Anthropic roster; after the all-free flip those seats became Gemini/Mistral
# and probes (2026-07-10) showed LiteLLM 1.88 silently DROPS `thinking` for
# them — zero reasoning tokens, i.e. the list was SUPPRESSING depth.
# reasoning_effort=high fires real Gemini thinking (verified: 385 reasoning
# tokens on pro-coder), so free seats stay OFF the list; only the explicit
# PAID Anthropic hatches keep native budgets.
SERGE_THINKING_SEATS=opus-paid,sonnet-paid,haiku-paid
# Auto-escalate genuinely-hard turns (architecture, concurrency/correctness bugs,
# security-critical work, deep root-cause reasoning) from the cheap workhorse to a
# stronger seat. Tight keyword heuristic in openaiShim.ts (latestHumanTurnIsHardTask);
# stays on the strong seat for the whole tool loop, flips back on the next easy human
# turn. 2026-07-09: retargeted pro-coder → cloud-brain (user call; pro-coder is now
# Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite, weaker than the Mistral workhorse — escalation went DOWN).
# cloud-brain = Gemini 3.5 Flash, strongest free seat, ~20 req/day bucket — sized for
# genuinely-hard frequency now that the shim strips injected <system-reminder> text.
# Only escalates FROM local-coder (override: SERGE_CLASSIFIER_FROM).
# Tune the trigger with SERGE_CLASSIFIER_REGEX; unset SERGE_CLASSIFIER_MODEL to disable.
# 2026-07-15: TRIED retargeting cloud-brain → think-coder (Magistral) for more hard-turn
# reasoning budget (cloud-brain is a thinking seat but ~20 req/day), then smoke-tested
# Magistral as an agentic DRIVER — because the classifier makes the target drive the
# whole tool loop. Result (clean in-cwd "read this file, reply with the number" task,
# warm router): Magistral did NOT issue the Read call — it emitted chat-style reasoning
# ("I'll work through it step-by-step... please provide the problem") and stalled to
# timeout, while local-coder (Mistral) answered "7391" correctly. Magistral is a
# reasoning model that does NOT reliably drive Claude Code's tool loop (same failure
# class the roster documents for Cerebras gpt-oss/GLM) — it is a READ-ONLY consultant
# (agents/think.md, /deepthink), never a driver. So the escalation target must both
# reason AND drive: a Gemini thinking seat. Kept cloud-brain (Gemini 3.5 Flash: thinks +
# drives; its fallback hops free-flash3/25/flash — all Gemini thinking seats, ~60/day
# combined — before ever degrading to the non-reasoning workhorse). The every-turn
# reasoning win lives in the always-on deliberate.md overlay on the proven Mistral
# driver, NOT in swapping the hard-turn seat to a non-driving reasoner.
SERGE_CLASSIFIER_MODEL=cloud-brain
# Broadened hard-task trigger (2026-06-26). The built-in HARD_TASK_DEFAULT keys only
# on architecture/concurrency/security vocabulary and missed 100% of practical-debug
# turns sampled from a real session ("error when clicked", "EPG overlap still there",
# "stream stall") — so genuine bug-hunting stayed on cheap Flash and reasoned poorly.
# This adds persistent-failure / practical-debug signals so those turns escalate to
# pro-coder (still cheap DeepSeek Pro, NOT Opus). Double-quoted so \b and the won'?t
# apostrophe survive sourcing. Invalid regex falls back to the default (openaiShim
# hardTaskRegex try/catch). Revert: delete this line (reverts to HARD_TASK_DEFAULT).
# 2026-07-17: added RESEARCH vocabulary (research/deep dive/investigate/compare/
# "what's the best"/alternatives/pros and cons/look into...) so research-shaped turns
# escalate to the thinking driver off the bat — the user wants reasoning + detailed
# synthesis by default on research asks, and cloud-brain (Gemini 3.5 Flash) both
# thinks and drives the search tool loop, still $0. Pairs with the constitution's
# research-depth rule and the new /research parallel panel. Cost: a research turn
# holds the ~20/day direct bucket (~60/day with Gemini fallback hops) for its tool
# loop; quota exhaustion degrades gracefully to the workhorse via router fallbacks.
SERGE_CLASSIFIER_REGEX="\b(architect(?:ure|ural|ing)?|re-?architect|re-?design|re-?structure|restructure|trade-?offs?|race conditions?|dead-?locks?|concurren(?:t|cy)|thread-?safe|data races?|memory leaks?|heisenbugs?|non-?deterministic|root[- ]cause|security (?:vulnerab|flaw|hole|review|audit)|vulnerabilit(?:y|ies)|exploit|sql injection|auth(?:n|z)? bypass|cryptograph(?:y|ic|ically)?|distributed (?:system|transaction|lock)|consensus algorithm|idempoten(?:t|cy|ce)?|formal(?:ly)? verif(?:y|ied|ication|ications)?|prove (?:that|why|it|the)|still (?:not|no) (?:work|working|showing|loading|rendering)|error when|throws?|crash(?:es|ing)?|stack ?trace|freez(?:e|es|ing)|stall(?:s|ing|ed)?|infinite loop|won'?t (?:load|render|build|compile|start)|keeps? (?:failing|crashing|breaking)|overlap (?:still|again)|regression|same (?:error|bug|issue) (?:again|still)|build (?:fail|error)|type ?error|research(?:ing|ed)?|deep[- ]?dive|in[- ]?depth|investigat(?:e|ing|ion)|compar(?:e|ing|ison)s?|versus|vs\.?|pros and cons|state of the art|alternatives? (?:to|for)|what(?:'?s| is| are) the best|which (?:is|one is) (?:better|best)|look into|options for|top (?:choices|options|picks|tools|libraries|frameworks))\b"

# ---- Auto-consult (native-reasoner pass on hard turns) ----------------------
# UserPromptSubmit hook (~/.serge/auto-consult.sh): on a turn matching the hard-task regex
# above, fire ONE reasoning_effort=high pass on think-coder (Magistral — the free native
# reasoner that reasons well but CANNOT drive the tool loop, verified 2026-07-15) and inject
# its analysis as turn context, so a PROVEN driver (Mistral/Gemini) runs the tools with a
# reasoner's prior in hand. The automatic form of /deepthink's consult. Easy turns: no-op.
# Fail-open: router-down / timeout / any error => the turn just proceeds.
#
# 2026-07-16 A/B (evals/reasoning-hard, REPS=5): OFF 23/25 vs ON 24/25 = within noise at
# ~3x turn latency on eval TRAPS — but 2026-07-17 the user explicitly reversed that trade
# ("reason harder — if he has to think a bit more to reason better, then do it"), so the
# consult is ON. It rides the big Mistral pool ($0, ~1B tok/mo) and fails open. Its trigger
# is now SERGE_CONSULT_REGEX below — the classifier vocab PLUS ambiguity/design signals —
# so intent-unclear turns get a "what is actually being asked" pass (the consult prompt
# extracts the real ask; targets the seen misread-intent failure) WITHOUT widening the
# cloud-brain escalation (still SERGE_CLASSIFIER_REGEX, its ~20/day bucket untouched).
# Set =0 to go back to fast-lean turns.
#
# 2026-07-29: added the "magic phrase" vocab — ultrathink / think step by step /
# think this through / reason harder|deeper|it through. Rationale: in THIS build
# `ultrathink` is a dead keyword (attachments.ts:1471 returns effort 'high', which
# is already what the workhorse gets after the xhigh→high clamp at effort.ts:290),
# yet theme.ts:79 rainbow-highlights it so it LOOKS like it did something. There is
# no "think harder"/"think step by step" keyword in the engine at all. Routing those
# phrases here makes them buy a real Magistral reasoning pass instead of nothing —
# serge's working substitute for stock Claude Code's extended-thinking scratchpad,
# which the non-reasoning workhorse (Mistral Large) does not have. $0 on every turn
# that doesn't match.
SERGE_AUTOCONSULT=1
SERGE_CONSULT_REGEX="${SERGE_CLASSIFIER_REGEX}|\b(how (?:should|would|do) (?:i|we|you)|what(?:'?s| is) the (?:right|best) way|best way to|not sure|unsure|confus(?:ed|ing)|ambiguous|what do you think|should (?:i|we) (?:use|go with|pick|choose)|design(?:ing)? (?:a|an|the)|approach(?:es)? (?:for|to)|strateg(?:y|ies) for|out[- ]of[- ]the[- ]box|think (?:harder|deeper|it through|this through|step by step)|ultrathink|reason (?:harder|deeper|it through)|figure out|make sense of)\b"
#   SERGE_CONSULT_MODEL=<seat>     # override the reasoning seat (default think-coder)
# Internal call cap (sec), kept < the hook's 90s timeout. Lowered 75→20 on
# 2026-07-29 for fluidity: a "hard" turn now waits at most ~20s for the pre-answer
# consult before failing open, instead of stalling up to 75s. Raise it back toward
# 75 if you want the reasoning seat to finish more often on genuinely hard turns.
# 2026-07-29 (later, user: "a tad more deeper when thinking, just a bit"): 20→30.
# At 20s Magistral often did NOT finish, so hard turns paid the full 20s AND failed
# open with no reasoning prior — worst of both. 30s buys the prior more often for
# +10s worst case, and only on regex-matched turns (easy turns still no-op).
# 2026-07-29 (same session, user: "put deliberate to 48 seconds"): 30→48. Still
# well under the hook's 90s timeout, so the consult is cut by THIS cap, not by the
# hook being killed mid-flight. Worst case a regex-matched turn now waits ~48s
# before answering; easy turns are untouched. Lower it here if that drags.
SERGE_CONSULT_MAXTIME=48

# ---- Verify-on-stop gate ----------------------------------------------------
# 0 = nudge-only: verify-on-stop.sh still runs typecheck/lint and reports, but a
# failure no longer exits 2 / re-runs the turn. (Default is enforce-always.)
SERGE_VERIFY_ENFORCE=0
# Interactive stops skip the soft full-test-suite pass (2026-07-18): it added
# up to SERGE_VERIFY_TEST_TIMEOUT=90s to the FIRST stop after every edit for
# an advisory-only signal. Typecheck/lint (scoped, blocking-capable) still
# run. Loops re-enable it (serge-loop.env) — unattended runs want the signal.
SERGE_VERIFY_TESTS=0

# ---- Eval-gate change detection ---------------------------------------------
# Files whose content the stop-gate hashes to detect a behavior-defining change.
# Overrides gate-on-stop.sh's default (which still names the old trimmed.md).
# The live constitution is now trimmed.v3.md (CLAUDE.md @-includes it) with the
# debugging doctrine split into debugging.md — so hash BOTH, or the stop-gate
# watches a dead file. Updated 2026-07-29 when v1/v2/CONSTITUTION.md were
# archived to backups/ (they were frozen decoys). `*` stays literal — the
# script word-splits and globs this unquoted.
SERGE_GATE_HASH_GLOBS="$HOME/.serge/CONSTITUTION.md $HOME/.serge/debugging.md $HOME/.serge/council.md $HOME/.serge/agents/*.md"

# ---- TUI renderer -----------------------------------------------------------
# Classic (main-screen) renderer. We tried the flicker-free alt-screen mode (=1)
# but on a tall terminal it left a large empty gap between the top content and
# the bottom-pinned input, and auto-scrolled the logo out of view. =0 keeps the
# compact inline look: the blue Clawd logo is visible at the top on startup and
# there's no gap. (Trade-off: with =0 the banner still scrolls away as the chat
# grows — a truly pinned header is a separate code change, not this toggle.)
CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER=0

# Raise the Bash tool default timeout 2min→5min so long builds/pipelines/test runs
# (npx tsx, bun build, full verify) complete in the foreground instead of being
# killed at 2m and looking "stuck" — which is what prompts the user to hit Esc.
# Genuinely long jobs should still use run_in_background. Tune/revert by editing
# this value (ms); delete the line to restore the 2-minute default.
BASH_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS=300000

# ---- Office+music toolchain (skills/office + skills/music, 2026-07-17) ------
# Shared venv backing the `office` skill (xlsx/docx/pptx/pdf: openpyxl, pandas,
# python-docx, python-pptx, pypdf, reportlab, pdfplumber, markitdown) AND the
# `music` skill (music21, mido, soundfile, scipy, python-osc, librosa-if-built).
# ONE venv on purpose: two venvs on PATH would break scripts importing across
# both stacks. Prepending its bin makes `python3`/`markitdown` in serge
# sessions resolve to the venv (Arch system python is externally-managed and
# bare, nothing lost). Pairs with system soffice (LibreOffice) + pdftoppm +
# ffmpeg. Deterministic local CPU tooling — no brick risk, $0, no network.
# Uninstall: delete this line + rm -rf ~/.serge/office-venv ~/.serge/skills/{office,music}.
PATH="$HOME/.serge/office-venv/bin:$PATH"

# ── eval-gate coverage for the ACTIVE constitution (added 2026-07-28) ─────────
# gate-on-stop.sh's default hash list still names CONSTITUTION.trimmed.v2.md; the
# brain moved to v3 (+ debugging.md) and v2 froze, so editing the live constitution
# stopped triggering any eval sweep. This routes the Stop-stage gate through a shim
# that supplies the correct list and then execs the real gate untouched.
# Revert: delete these two lines (gate-on-stop.sh itself was never modified).
SERGE_GATE_STOP_SCRIPT="$HOME/.serge/gate-on-stop-globs.sh"

# ── runtime feature-flag overrides stay inside serge's config dir (2026-08-14) ─
# src/services/analytics/growthbook.ts resolves the override file as
#   CLAUDE_FEATURE_FLAGS_FILE || join(homedir(), '.claude', 'feature-flags.json')
# — hardcoded to ~/.claude via homedir(), the ONE path in the engine that does not
# honour CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. The launcher pins CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=~/.serge precisely
# so serge and real Claude Code cannot touch each other's state, so without this
# line the first runtime gate anyone overrides would be written into the OTHER
# tool's config dir — and would change that tool's behaviour too.
# Neither file exists today, so this changes nothing now; it closes the trap
# before someone falls into it. A missing file is caught and ignored by
# _loadFlags(), which then falls through to _openBuildDefaults exactly as now.
# NOTE: this file only governs RUNTIME gates (the tengu_* names). Build-time
# feature() macros are fixed at bundle time by scripts/build.ts and cannot be
# changed from here — see the dead-letter note in growthbook.ts.
CLAUDE_FEATURE_FLAGS_FILE="$HOME/.serge/feature-flags.json"
